---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_NAMES, SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Privacy policy of ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: your inputs stay in your browser`} description="What personal data this sales tax and property tax calculator processes: server logs and Microsoft Clarity analytics with opt-out. Legal basis, retention and your US and EU rights." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This policy covers {SITE_URL}. The publisher is established in France, so the EU General Data Protection Regulation applies to everything the site does, whoever the visitor is. Visitors in US states with a consumer privacy law (California and others) have at least the rights described below.</p>
    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <h2>2. What the calculators never send</h2>
    <p>Prices, local rates, home values, mill rates and states you enter are processed in your browser only. They are not sent to a server, not stored by us and not linked to you. The share link writes your inputs into the page address: only send it to people you choose.</p>
    <h2>3. What is processed</h2>
    <h3>Server logs</h3><p>The host records the IP address, time, page requested and browser, for security. Legal basis: legitimate interest. Retention: according to GitHub's policy.</p>
    <h3>Audience measurement: Microsoft Clarity</h3><p>The site uses Microsoft Clarity (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, One Microsoft Place, Dublin) to understand which pages are useful. It processes clicks, scrolling, the pages viewed with their address, device and browser type and an approximate location derived from the IP address; the figures you enter are masked in the browser. A notice on your first visit tells you and lets you opt out; legal basis: legitimate interest in improving the site (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR), and opting out is your objection. Microsoft keeps recordings for 30 days and aggregated data for up to 13 months. Cookie details: <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a>.</p>
    <h3>E-mails</h3><p>If you write to us, your address and message are kept to answer you, for three years after the last exchange.</p>
    <h2>4. Sale or sharing of personal information</h2><p>We do not sell or share personal information, for money or otherwise, and we do not use it for targeted advertising. Microsoft receives Clarity data only to provide the analytics service to us.</p>
    <h2>5. Recipients and transfers</h2><p>The host, GitHub, Inc., and Microsoft, for Clarity, are in the United States; data may be processed there under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework.</p>
    <h2>6. Your rights</h2><p>Access, correction, deletion, restriction, objection and portability: write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; we reply within one month. You can complain to the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>).</p>
    <h2>7. Children</h2><p>The site is not directed at children under 13 and collects nothing from them.</p>
    <p>See also the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
